  "term": "motivational interviewing",
  "definition": "Motivational interviewing is a client-centered but guiding counselling method that aims to help a person find their own motivation to change. It uses open questions, reflective listening, and a nonjudgmental, nonconfrontational style to encourage open discussion and reduce resistance around risky or problem behavior.",
